  - { id: ~note1, type: Note, name: SysML PACKAGE reuses UML package notation exactl…, documentation: 'SysML PACKAGE reuses UML package notation exactly:\nthe folder/tab glyph, nesting, «import»/«access»\nstereotypes, and dependency arrows are identical.\nThe ONLY difference is the CONTENTS — SysML\npackages hold «block», «valueType», «requirement»\nelements; UML packages hold generic classes,\ndata types, and constraints. The projection\n(layout + relationships) is the same.' }
edges:
